## Control {{controlId}}: Verify and Control Connections to External Systems

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization verifies and controls all connections to external information systems within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. External system connections are managed through Azure AD cross-tenant access policies, B2B collaboration settings, and Conditional Access policies that restrict external sharing and guest access to authorized organizations only.

{{#if crossTenantPolicyConfigured}}
Azure AD cross-tenant access policies are configured to control inbound and outbound connections. Default B2B collaboration settings restrict external sharing to pre-approved organizations. Guest user access is governed by cross-tenant trust relationships that define which external tenants may authenticate and access resources. Each external connection is documented and reviewed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}} prior to approval.
{{else}}
Azure AD cross-tenant access policies have not been configured. External system connections are not restricted beyond default Azure AD settings, pending policy implementation.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
Conditional Access policies enforce additional external connection controls:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}} for external access scenarios.
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Review Azure AD cross-tenant access policy configurations, B2B collaboration settings, and guest user access logs to verify external connection controls.

